## Ownership

- Shared and durable: edit `home/...` in a worktree of `~/src/boilerplate`,
  preview with `chezmoi -S <worktree> diff`, commit, land, and reconcile
  (`decent-angl-config`).
- Machine-local or OS-owned: change the live setting on the target host.
- Home router, firewall, DHCP, or DNS appliance state: use `opnsense`.
- Inspect where a value lives before deciding ownership.

Common shared state includes shells, agent harnesses, terminals, Omarchy desktop
overrides, and shipped user services. Input speed, display scaling, battery
policy, Bluetooth pairing, and app login state are normally machine-local.

For Omarchy/Linux work, read [references/omarchy.md](references/omarchy.md).
For macOS work, read [references/macos.md](references/macos.md).
For the inference-only host `nous`, read [references/nous.md](references/nous.md).
For game streaming from `wincube` (Apollo host; Moonlight/Artemis client settings per
device, Wake-on-LAN), read [references/wincube-streaming.md](references/wincube-streaming.md).
For the second host `winbox` (Rhode Island; RTX 4090, `ssh winbox`, `wake winbox`, computer use,
measured bitrates), read [references/winbox-streaming.md](references/winbox-streaming.md).

## Completion

Re-read each changed setting or file. For shared changes, verify rendered live
output after reconcile applies the landed commit. Report any required logout, reconnect, reload,
or restart.
